1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,320
Yes, for the changes in our production plans, excluding unpredictable events, those related to nature and random events. We do not plan any changes here in terms of our production.

2
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:29,980
And we have already seen the first outcomes. We were able to reduce energy consumption with the same production parameters as we used to have.

3
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:46,700
Most importantly, a year into our partnership with GA, we couldn't feel any better about our collective progress, including the performance of management, the profitability of our stake, scaling of the AUM, and the integration of our teams.

4
00:00:47,440 --> 00:01:02,440
I will pass it on to Lisa to comment on margin, but just to clarify my comments, I said when we passed prices, we passed on prices to make sure that we protect our...

5
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:17,000
This is, again, a first step into a continued modernization journey for entertainment business that, again, in the end should be able to stabilize the total TV line over time.

6
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:27,920
And really, the key for us is to take our leading position there with our leading position across infrastructure, real estate, credit growth, equity on a global basis, and the marriage of those two things.

7
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:31,120
And we think that could lead to a lot of growth for us in that part of the world.

8
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:45,960
You know, I think the big advantage here is we come into 2022 with over $15 billion of embedded revenue that sits in our balance sheet between gross and realized carry and the embedded gains of our investment portfolio.

9
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:56,080
So, from now on, any update will be called patch, and if there will be any hot fixes.

10
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:07,560
So, going from a quite significant negative trend in B2B to being a stable business was what we said we would do, and we've done it.

11
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:17,140
Ladies and gentlemen, the subject you have brought up concerns one of the assets, which is now in the process of sale.

12
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:27,920
And if you see any major impact to the product that you and your peers are providing to insurance clients.

13
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:30,100
Market.

14
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:38,620
Latin America reported 8% organic growth, of which approximately one-third came from euro pricing.

15
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:49,960
In Sweden Consumer, we continued our more-for-more strategy and saw strong performance within mobile postpaid and fixed broadband, while we were able to mitigate the decline in digital TV.

16
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:54,020
But you are right, it's still a very volatile environment.

17
00:02:54,020 --> 00:03:00,420
So, I think we're only, let's say, three months into the year of 12 months.

18
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:10,360
But one of the things it brings is a deep understanding, not only of mobile markets, and not only of broadband markets, but also the TV side of the business.

19
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:20,560
So, I would be happy to find out what is the management board's view of what the value might be in the third quarter or in the second half of the year.

20
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:30,660
Because, as you think, especially as Global Atlantic pursues block activity, we're bringing on more assets, and then those blocks need to be rotated themselves.

21
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:39,120
And then, of course, it will vary over time where the biggest contribution comes from.

22
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:47,520
Thus, our international transactions increased 120% sequentially, coming from very low levels.

23
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:54,540
That is, will one-off change in next year's dividend or not?

24
00:03:55,900 --> 00:04:01,780
We closed the quarter with a solid cash position of $276 million.

25
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:06,680
Nothing bombastic, so to say.

26
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:18,440
The initial ambition last quarter to reflect the divestment of natural colors and the acquisition of genuine.

27
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:27,780
And then I wonder what this implies for the HMO revenue in the quarter.

28
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:35,440
Meaning that if orders were to grow around 100, okay, structural costs should be growing no more than 40%.

29
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:42,940
And this is one of the sunniest places in the world, and on the top of it, it is completely empty.

30
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:50,720
Mobile net intake continued to be strong in the quarter, driven by new contracts, both within SME and large segments.

31
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:51,860
Thank you.

